1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:02,980
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure!

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:06,757
I don't think I'm going to
be able to help you, folks.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,899
It's been my job to repair rooftops
in Cairo for around 40 years now.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:14,296
And I can't say that I've
ever seen a place like this.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,871
And my daughter's condition is much worse.

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:19,432
At best, she has three or four days left.

7
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,400
I can almost feel it.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,659
It's like Dio's right on top of us.

9
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,395
We should get moving.

10
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,286
We'll talk to everyone
here until we find him.

11
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,520
It's a real scorcher out here today.

12
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,020
I haven't had a shower in almost two days.

13
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,911
It's beginning to ruin my je ne Suzi Quee.

14
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,470
Huh?

15
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,120
Uh... Hmm.

16
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:01,770
Huh?

17
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,660
What's the big idea, asshole?

18
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,337
You got some kind of problem with me?

19
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:22,137
I've got a problem with
where you're sitting!

20
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:24,317
A cocky foreigner like you has no business

21
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,597
sitting here pretending
to be some kind of beggar!

22
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,997
Don't you have a lick of common sense?

23
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,400
Who said that you could sit here, huh?

24
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,387
Ah, you must be a beggar
from a foreign land.

25
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,149
I know this isn't much
But I hope it helps.

26
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,040
Thanks, but

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,060
You back off pal.

28
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,161
This is my turf.

29
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,789
You poofy-haired blockhead

30
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:49,160
What's that supposed to hey hold a wrap?

31
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:54,660
Don't just sit there with your mouth agape
give that money to him immediately Hmm?

32
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,360
Oh, I get what's going
on here. He's a beggar.

33
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,877
You'll have to forgive my
friend's obliviousness.

34
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,497
He's not accustomed to
the rules of this city.

35
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:07,397
Why didn't you tell me you were
a beggar in the first place?

36
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,497
It's called having a shtick, you numbnut.

37
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,597
People around here know
me as a mute beggar.

38
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:14,757
There's something known as
a beggar's association here.

39
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,717
Beggars have their own
areas where they're paid

40
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,117
to do nothing but sit
around and beg all day.

41
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:20,937
While it may seem strange to us,

42
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,277
the rules they put in place help
keep everything running smoothly.

43
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,340
Get out.

44
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:28,957
Yes, and that exchange from
earlier has hurt my pride.

45
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:33,277
I wonder if I'd make more money by
disguising myself as a foreign beggar.

46
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,597
The hobos, they are a changin'.

47
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:40,017
Oh, by the way, I thought I
recognized you from somewhere.

48
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,117
If I'm not mistaken, you're
Avdol the fortune teller.

49
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,440
Way I hear it, you got
spooked and fled to Japan.

50
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,277
Apparently, someone was
looking to kill you.

51
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:52,437
I'd rather discuss us needing
a favor from the one who knows

52
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:56,696
everything there is to know about
this area you'll be well compensated.

53
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:03,657
It's imperative that we find this
building as quickly as possible.

54
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,269
We're running out of time.

55
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,540
I've done enough work for one day.

56
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,844
You gents have my word that I'll
find the mansion in three hours.

57
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:25,920
Just sit tight.

58
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,720
By the way, did anyone
see where Iggy ran off to?

59
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,471
Oh no, I don't even know.

60
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:21,080
This is a series of videos.

61
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:23,160
I'm going to play with you.

62
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,400
Stop it now.

63
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:32,905
The explosion of the
world for this long story.

64
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,837
I'm going to show you now.

65
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,840
I'm going to continue the next episode.

66
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,800
I'm going to play with you.

67
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:48,060
I'm going to hang out with you.

68
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:49,950
Come back!

69
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:50,920
End of the war!

70
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,417
Hora! Hora! Hora! Hora! Hora!

71
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,330
Hora!

72
00:05:02,413 --> 00:05:03,243
Hora! Hora!

73
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:33,920
Oh, my God.

74
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:48,890
Dad!

75
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,380
No!

76
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,150
Hmm.

77
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:58,290
Hmm.

78
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,210
Huh?

79
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,480
Let's go.

80
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:04,557
That's the place all right mission
accomplished and it only took two hours.

81
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:08,420
If it exists in this city you
can bet your ass I'll find it.

82
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:29,480
Iggy thought to himself, So that
bird is a stand user, same as me.

83
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:32,917
Given that it offed that guy
with a giant block of ice,

84
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,897
it must be the guard around here.

85
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:37,627
It'll kill anyone who
approaches the mansion.

86
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:43,440
Which means that bird's next
target is probably gonna be me.

87
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,240
From early on,

88
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,897
the ancient Egyptians
recognized the prowess of

89
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:57,017
the noble falcon soaring
high above the Nile Valley.

90
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:01,335
They trained the bird as a hunting
partner and considered it a symbol of

91
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,397
Horus, guardian deity of the royal family.

92
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:08,880
The falcon's vision is able to spot
prey from several kilometers away.

93
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:12,237
Its oculus is forever
represented by the eye of Horus,

94
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,880
an emblem of protection and royal power.

95
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,976
The falcon soaring through
the air is called Pet Shop.

96
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:22,820
It is the wielder of the
Stand Horus, God of the Sky.

97
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,480
Nervously, Iggy thought, Damn it.

98
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,080
This is just my luck.

99
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,694
Looks like I stumbled on Dio's mansion.

100
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:34,508
Why'd I have to find this place
instead of one of the others?

101
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:38,980
What's worse, that falcon can use its
stand to shoot giant chunks of ice.

102
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,435
It's like a super-powered god, though.

103
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,015
Actually, it's more like a guard bird.

104
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:53,960
Come on.

105
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,417
You gotta be kidding me.

106
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,853
I couldn't care less about this Tio guy.

107
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,840
I got dragged here against my will.

108
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,397
Like some head and forced to
be one of the Joestar's allies.

109
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,656
Like hell I'm gonna fight this thing.

110
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,605
All I want is a little Aranar.

111
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:09,617
A girl of my own.

112
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,229
Some place to settle down.

113
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:15,157
Fighting someone else's battle
isn't on my list of things to do.

114
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:18,677
Besides, even if I were to throw
down with Tweety over there,

115
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,117
what would I get in return?

116
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,837
There's no way I'm putting
my life on the line.

117
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:25,457
Time to bring out that
old dumb dog routine.

118
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:28,834
That bird brain will never
suspect them with those guys.

119
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:56,750
Those eyes.

120
00:09:56,833 --> 00:09:58,117
That's the thing about birds.

121
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,597
You can never tell what they're thinking!

122
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,520
I bet my stand could take him.

123
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:05,837
But then again, there's a reason I'm
making a fool out of myself here.

124
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:08,777
I've got nothing to do with
Jotaro and those other guys.

125
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:11,507
Go back to your mansion,
you feathered freak.

126
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,600
Huh? A bird?

127
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,060
What's with this bird?

128
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:25,440
Why isn't the damn thing moving?

129
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,777
No, it's too late.

130
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,154
I'm gonna run it over.

131
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,630
Huh?

132
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:41,917
I've never seen anything
like that bird in my life.

133
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,941
How could it fly under a
car so low to the ground?

134
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,837
It didn't even try to
dodge out of the way.

135
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:50,449
It dove without giving
it a second thought.

136
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:53,860
Crazy bastard.

137
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,772
But it seems like the freaks
lost interest to me, for now.

138
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:00,490
Apparently,

139
00:11:00,573 --> 00:11:04,577
it only goes on the offensive when people
try to make their way inside the mansion.

140
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:08,740
Even so, if Jotaro and the others
ever end up finding this place,

141
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,845
they'll have a hell of
a time trying to get in.

142
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,029
Oh well, that's their
problem to deal with.

143
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,080
Butch! Tiny!

144
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,200
Butch! Tiny!

145
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,616
Where'd you guys go?

146
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:25,745
Hey, you haven't seen my
dogs around, have you?

147
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,397
Their names are Butch and
Tiny, if that helps at all.

148
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,600
Get the hell out of my face!

149
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,020
I'm a dog, pal!

150
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:34,637
Well, even if I knew, it's
not like I could answer.

151
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,955
What are you, stupid?

152
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:40,320
Oh, no!

153
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,151
That collar looks like...

154
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:44,820
I was right, it's Tiny's!

155
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:47,826
I don't understand, why
is it under this gate?

156
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,966
And why is there blood on it?

157
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:53,460
Tiny and Butch, is he
talking about those big dogs?

158
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:56,100
Tiny! Butch!

159
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:58,177
What's that kid thinking?

160
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,937
If he tries going under the gate, he'll
have to face the wrath of that bird!

161
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:05,620
It'll murder him! Tiny!
Butch! Are you there?

162
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,500
Tiny! Butch!

163
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,320
Tiny! Butch!

164
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:15,957
I don't know why I'm getting so worked up.

165
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:19,440
If some human kid bites a
big one, it's not my problem.

166
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:22,316
Survival of the fittest, as they say.

167
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,780
Stupid die first, as do
people who act recklessly.

168
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:30,040
I'd rather stay out of
this, so... Goodbye, kid.

169
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,980
Tiny! Butch, come out! This isn't funny!

170
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:35,880
I'm here to take you home!

171
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,360
Holy shit!

172
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:18,920
Good grief.

173
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,220
I have a soft spot for kid dog lovers.

174
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,960
Lucky for him.

175
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:53,920
I didn't want to get involved,
but it's up to me now!

176
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:05,037
He had finally revealed his stand,
confirming Pet Shop's suspicions?

177
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,708
about Iggy's extraordinary
canine abilities.

178
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:09,280
Bring it, Feather Boy!

179
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,780
I can't wait to rip you to shreds!

180
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,377
The falcon is known for its ability.

181
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:18,520
To dive at speeds of over
300 kilometers per hour,

182
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:21,369
making it the fastest
animal on the planet.

183
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:26,500
Even at its trademark speed, the Falcon
can spot its quarry with pinpoint accuracy.

184
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:31,840
The prey, once discovered, faces a violent
death by way of razor-sharp talons!

185
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,210
Huh?

186
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,380
What the?

187
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,200
Did he just smirk at me?

188
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:46,152
I could have sworn I saw the
corners of its beak creep up.

189
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:49,000
But birds can't smile, can they?

190
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,300
Wait, what's going on here?

191
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:56,480
The air, it's getting colder!

192
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,050
Hmm!

193
00:15:01,133 --> 00:15:02,637
Ice is coming out of the ground!

194
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,779
I'm such an idiot!

195
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:07,737
I was so focused on the bird, I didn't
realize my feet were frozen over!

196
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,460
My stance feet froze too!

197
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,070
Shit!

198
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,030
Icicles!

199
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,574
Come on, give it to me straight, Avdol.

200
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:51,577
Do you honestly believe that guy has
any chance of finding Dio's mansion?

201
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,377
I certainly hope so,
because if he can't find it,

202
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,737
there's no one left in the city who can.

203
00:15:56,820 --> 00:16:00,257
No one knows Cairo's complex
maze of streets better than him.

204
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,752
Try and have some faith.

205
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,197
Faith is something I'm
quickly running out of.

206
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:07,997
We've been looking around this godforsaken
city for three days with no luck.

207
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:11,337
I highly doubt some beggar will
find the mansion in three hours.

208
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:14,077
You're starting to sound like
a broken record, Polnareff.

209
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,157
You could at least try
to keep a level head.

210
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:17,070
Listen up.

211
00:16:17,153 --> 00:16:18,537
We're all on edge right now.

212
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:22,417
Until our friend gets back, all we
can do is try talking to the locals.

213
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,337
Oh, brother.

214
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:26,714
And to make matters worse,
we haven't seen Iggy all day.

215
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,297
Where the hell did that
stupid mutt run off to?

216
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,840
He better not be lost.

217
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,317
For as long as I've known him, Iggy's
always been somewhat of a loner.

218
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,817
So I'm sure he's just
wandering around somewhere,

219
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:39,076
killing time before coming back home.

220
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:43,717
I used to think all dogs lit up and
wag their tails when they saw humans.

221
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,271
How'd we get stuck with that little cynic?

222
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,935
I managed to get away from it somehow.

223
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:59,675
It's Stan's ice attack took
the skin right off my paws.

224
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:04,477
Damn it, I knew I should have let
that human kid fix his own problems!

225
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,557
It's Stan's power is nothing to sneeze at.

226
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,420
That was no ordinary ice?

227
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,518
And I bet he still has a few tricks.

228
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,801
I better get out of here
while the getting's good.

229
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:37,620
Talk about holding a grudge!

230
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:46,960
Highway!

231
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:02,100
Iggy disappeared, but
where could he have gone?

232
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,660
Damn it. That hurt.

233
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:13,652
The best that doesn't hold anything back.

234
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,700
He's strong for a dumb bird

235
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,757
This place reeks but
it'll have to do for now.

236
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:25,428
I have to keep quiet and hide
out down here until he gives up

237
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:50,090
Hey!

238
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:54,690
Surprise!

239
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,977
Thought you had me, didn't you?

240
00:18:57,060 --> 00:19:00,472
But what you killed was my
shape-shifting stand, the fool!

241
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:05,610
Yeah!

242
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,471
How do you like them apples, Featherbrain?

243
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,491
Might want to keep still.

244
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:19,037
Looks like you're losing
a lot of blood there.

245
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,157
But before this drags out any further,

246
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:25,597
you should probably know I don't give a
rat's ass about you or your master deal.

247
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:27,798
What do you say we call this a draw?

248
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:32,494
You got a few good hits in with those
ice missiles, so we're even, right?

249
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:38,540
What the hell was that?

250
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,192
Who does this guy think he is, Bruce Lee?

251
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:43,180
Hey! Can't you hear?

252
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:45,637
I said I'll stay away
from your boss's mansion!

253
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,180
Let's stop this, okay?

254
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:49,130
Huh?

255
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:01,930
Huh?

256
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,861
That's what your skin looks like?

257
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:13,780
What am I gonna do now?

258
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:22,277
You stopped your wound from
bleeding by freezing it?

259
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:24,000
What the hell? Ah!

260
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:25,410
Last it!

261
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:28,020
Oh no, the exit's blocked with ice!

262
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,888
Everyone's coming this way!

263
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:32,430
Shit!

264
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,618
It's time to cover the whole tunnel!

265
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:39,451
I gotta find a way out of this death trap!

266
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,020
Ah! No way!

267
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:55,002
It blocked off this engine, too!

268
00:20:57,620 --> 00:20:58,450
Ah!

269
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,250
Ah!

270
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:07,970
Crap.

271
00:21:08,053 --> 00:21:09,497
It's got me in its crosshairs.

272
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:10,720
This bird's insane!

273
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:13,517
This is more than sheer determination.

274
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:15,857
This creep's a freaking killing machine!

275
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,137
And if it catches me,
it won't just kill me.

276
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:19,800
It'll leave me alive!

277
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,480
What?

278
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:33,760
No, it's my ball!

279
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:37,860
I can't fret my pull-a-loose!

280
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:20,400
Thank you.

281
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,460
Thank you.

282
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,217
Transcription

283
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:32,260
by CastingWords
